# The 32-bit field subtraction carries ctutils::Choice across nine limbs rather
# than converting each outgoing borrow to a mask and immediately back again.
# All nine protected subtraction primitives and the final protected mask remain.
# crypto-bigint 0.7.6 and ctutils 0.4.5 security fixes remain required by the locks.
# No change to the masked modulus add-back or the 64-bit field implementation.
# sub_inner is visible only to its parent for the normal rsk-ec host32 tests,
# which compile this exact source and compare it with wide arithmetic/field64.
#
# The correction is always inlined so modulus operands stay constant and
# no three-array call boundary is introduced by the protected primitives.
#
# 32-bit squaring specializes crypto-bigint 0.7.6 schoolbook::square_wide for
# eight words: 28 fixed-index cross products, the same shift and eight diagonal
# products with carries, then unchanged Montgomery reduction. Its Apache/MIT
# upstream origin is retained in crypto-bigint.patch. The 64-bit path is unchanged.
